>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (EduLearn is an educational platform website developed to provide learners with a structured and user-friendly online interface for exploring educational content and courses. The website is designed around the idea of making learning information accessible through a clear layout, organized pages and interactive features. It includes six interconnected pages: Home, About, Courses, Blog, Contact and Login/Signup. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The project was implemented using HTML5, CSS3 and JavaScript. HTML5 provides the structure and semantic organization of the pages, CSS3 is used for styling, responsive layouts, transitions and animations, and JavaScript manages interactive behavior such as course rendering, category filtering, search, testimonial navigation, form validation, blog loading and simulated login/signup behavior. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The Courses page presents course cards and supports category-based filtering and search. The Blog page displays articles and provides a Load More interaction. The Contact page contains contact information and a validated contact form, while the Login/Signup page provides tab switching, password visibility controls and client-side validation. Browser localStorage is used for simulated authentication state; the project is a client-side website and does not include a production backend or server-side database. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (The project demonstrates the practical application of frontend web development concepts, responsive design, DOM manipulation, event handling and client-side data handling. It also provides a foundation for future development, including backend integration, secure authentication, course enrollment, learning progress tracking and mobile application support. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
